### LO5 - API Testing Evidence (Alternative to Postman)
### You can take a screenshot of this file to show your API Testing!

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

# Paste/Update your access token here if the endpoint needs auth
@accessToken = {{ $dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN }}


---
### 1. GET ALL PRODUCTS
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Accept: application/json

###

---
### 2. GET SINGLE PRODUCT
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/product/Moringa
Accept: application/json

###

---
### 3. GET COMPANY INFO
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/info
Accept: application/json

###

---
### 4. POST AI CHATBOT MESSAGE
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What are the benefits of Shilajit?"
}

###

---
### 5. POST FEEDBACK
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/feedback
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "rating": 5,
  "message": "This is a test feedback from API testing."
}

###

---
### 5b. (Update example) POST /api/admin/users/{user_id}/role  (admin/staff only)
# Your code updates user role via POST (not HTTP PUT)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/1/role
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "staff"
}

###


---
### 6. GET FEEDBACK LIST
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/feedback
Accept: application/json

###

---
### 7. POST REGISTER USER
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json


{
  "full_name": "API Test User",
  "email": "apitest@example.com",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

###

---
### 8. POST LOGIN USER
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=apitest@example.com&password=securepassword123

